{
  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "5482",
      "field": "detail",
      "english": "So you can see the predicament that I'm in, <Name>. That thing is out there collecting the wrong weeds! I'll make it worth your while to gather what I need. Bring back to me enough doom weed and I'll give you a suitable reward.\n\nIt is my understanding that they like to plague the flora near the mass gravesite, to the north of the Brill graveyard. Hurry and be mindful of the gnolls in the area."
    },
    {
      "id": "5482",
      "field": "objective",
      "english": "Collect 10 Doom Weed and deliver them back to Junior Apothecary Holland."
    },
    {
      "id": "5482",
      "field": "progress",
      "english": "This had better be good. I trust you have all of the doom weed that I require?"
    },
    {
      "id": "5482",
      "field": "complete",
      "english": "Ah, my doom weed. Excellent!\n\n<Junior Apothecary Holland rubs his hands together greedily.>\n\nThese will come in quite handy. You've done me, uh, the Lady, a fine service today <name>. As promised here is the reward that you deserve."
    },
    {
      "id": "5650",
      "field": "title",
      "english": "Garments of Darkness"
    },
    {
      "id": "5650",
      "field": "detail",
      "english": "Our power comes from darkness and shadow, <name>, but that is not your only role. You have acknowledged that there is merit in knowing the healing arts. This is wise. But before you can know the dark, you must also know the light. And for this, I have a test for you.\n\nNorth of the cemetery is a wounded Deathguard--Deathguard Kel. He has protected us from gnolls for some time, and needs healing. But, you must also fortify his body before he can return to duty. Do both with your spells, and then return to me."
    },
    {
      "id": "5650",
      "field": "objective",
      "english": "Find Deathguard Kel and heal his wounds using Lesser Heal (Rank 2). Afterwards, grant him Power Word: Fortitude and then return to Dark Cleric Beryl in Brill."
    },
    {
      "id": "5650",
      "field": "progress",
      "english": "Our powers make us ideal for so many situations, <name>. You'll find that no matter what though, our ability to mend wounds and increase the amount of damage our companions can take will always be the most desired talents we have access to. Do not let that dissuade you from pursuing other paths as a <class>--you can be effective in many ways. But... if you truly wish to destroy your enemies with magical energy, perhaps the arcane is more to your liking."
    },
    {
      "id": "5650",
      "field": "complete",
      "english": "You have passed my test with ease. Good.\n\nSoon, you will be ready to take on more responsibility and that road will lead to darker powers--powers that no <class> of another race has.\n\nTake this robe as a symbol of your station. You have earned it. If you do not wish to wear it, then so be it, you may do with it as you will. I and others like us will always acknowledge you for what you've achieved in our ranks."
    },
    {
      "id": "86784",
      "field": "title",
      "english": "Sticks and Bones"
    },
    {
      "id": "86784",
      "field": "detail",
      "english": "My associate Eleanor Shackleton prides herself on traveling the wilds, surviving against weather and monsters. She is currently camped not far from here, in the hills to the west, and I remember a piece of advice that she once gave me: \"When you think you have enough firewood, gather five times more.\"\n\nIf you have some spare time, you could collect some wood in this basket and take it to her camp. I'm sure she could give you a few tips about the existence of a traveling adventurer."
    },
    {
      "id": "86784",
      "field": "objective",
      "english": "Collect 6 Dry Branches and bring them to Eleanor Shackleton."
    },
    {
      "id": "91282",
      "field": "title",
      "english": "A Second Home"
    },
    {
      "id": "91282",
      "field": "detail",
      "english": "It is encouraging to see my newly risen brothers and sisters thrive as you have. It is only through community and shared faith that we can truly realize our full potential however, and to that end we've begun to form a new paladin order right here in Tirisfal. \n\nIf you wish to learn more, you should visit our monastery on the edge of the Whispering Woods. It is called Bandarion Keep. It's on the bluffs just northwest of the Solliden Farmstead, and should be hard to miss."
    },
    {
      "id": "91282",
      "field": "objective",
      "english": "Find the fortress of Bandarion Keep and report to Breton Samuels there."
    },
    {
      "id": "91285",
      "field": "title",
      "english": "Murlocs at the Gates"
    },
    {
      "id": "91285",
      "field": "detail",
      "english": "Normally we'd show our newcomers a bit more hospitality, but we've got a bit of a murloc problem at the moment.\n\nA tribe of murlocs used to use the keep as their spawning grounds. They've been a problem since we moved in and kicked them out, but now it's starting to get out of hand. You look like you've seen some action. Do you think you could help us drive back some of these pests? You'll find them lurking in the bluffs along the road to the east, and in the camps around the lake to the west."
    },
    {
      "id": "91285",
      "field": "objective",
      "english": "Slay 8 Vile Fin Attackers and 8 Vile Fin Seers and report back to Breton Samuels when it is done."
    },
    {
      "id": "91294",
      "field": "title",
      "english": "Touring the Grounds"
    },
    {
      "id": "91294",
      "field": "detail",
      "english": "Now that the immediate threat of the murloc attacks is under control, I'd encourage you to show yourself around our stronghold. It isn't much yet, but it's home.\n\nWhen you are done exploring, seek out Danitha Morr, our leader. She can help you get settled in.\n\nI'm very glad to have met you, <Name>. May the light be your guide."
    },
    {
      "id": "91294",
      "field": "objective",
      "english": "Speak to the residents of Bandarion Keep."
    },
    {
      "id": "91316",
      "field": "title",
      "english": "Making Repairs"
    }
  ],
  "response": {
